From e31388412c7cb2b21725c0ff8a306ac144c4b642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kdsuomi <kdsuomi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:43:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(tui): measure stream rate from attributed chunk
 arrivals

The stream numerator previously took each response's full exact usage
(including hidden reasoning and never-streamed terminal payloads) while
its denominator covered only the observed delta window, inflating the
displayed rate by up to 10x. The stream rate is now computed purely from
delta arrivals: each chunk's estimated tokens are attributed to the
interval since the previous chunk (the first chunk of a response only
starts the clock), aggregated over a rolling 10s window that decays
through stalls, with a whole-turn cumulative figure retained at turn
end. Exact usage feeds only the API rate and the chars-per-token
calibration, which is now keyed per model and per output category and
skips samples whose char and token sides cover different output. The
status line repaints on a 250ms cadence while a turn runs so a stalled
stream visibly decays.
